{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["iOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"@","kind":"attribute"},{"text":"MainActor","kind":"attribute","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"init","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}]}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview\/init()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"init","externalID":"s:5Swami20Interaction_DragViewVACycfc","role":"symbol","title":"init()","roleHeading":"Initializer","modules":[{"name":"Swami"}],"fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}]},"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView\/init()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView"]]},"references":{"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction_DragView/init()":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview\/init()","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView\/init()","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[],"fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"title":"init()"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction_DragView":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Interaction_DragView"}],"title":"Interaction_DragView","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview","abstract":[{"text":"Drags a layer in any direction with momentum and rubber-band bounds. The draggable","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"card responds to touch input via Origami’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"origami.Drag","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" patch, which wires its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"output ","type":"text"},{"code":"Position","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to the layer’s transform. When released near the center, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"card snaps back to its resting position.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Interaction_DragView"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"kind":"symbol","title":"Swami","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"code":".origami","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swami"}}}